m\"}],\"synopsis\":\"<p>Waterstones Romford and Lumiere Romford are proud to present an evening with author Jay Glennie, and a screening of Quentin Tarantino's Inglourious Basterds.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li><strong>6pm - Q&A and signing session with Jay Glennie<\\/strong>, author of The Making of Quentin Tarantino's Inglourious Basterds.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li><strong>Approx 7:30pm<\\/strong> - After the Q&A, enjoy a showing of the film on the big screen!<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p><span style=\\\"text-decoration: underline;\\\"><strong>About the book<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\r\\n<p>A stunning and faithful deep dive into the mind of a masterful auteur and a must-have book for all film lovers and Quentin Tarantino fans alike.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>In the definitive and official examination of legendary filmmaker Quentin Tarantino&rsquo;s Inglourious Basterds, writer Jay Glennie pulls back the curtain on the visionary writer, director, and producer&rsquo;s sixth film, with unprecedented access to the filmmaker, cast, and crew. Pore over 400 pages detailing every aspect of the film, from the writing of the script, casting, rehearsals, through to production and costume design, the making of the film, and beyond.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>Featuring an exclusive foreword by Brad Pitt, this comprehensive volume offers an unparalleled look into the making of Inglourious Basterds through never-before-seen pieces of concept art, behind-the-scenes photography, rare documents from the personal archives of Tarantino and producer Lawrence Bender, and much more.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p><span style=\\\"text-decoration: underline;\\\"><strong>About the film<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\r\\n<p>In Nazi-occupied France during World War II, a group of Jewish-American soldiers known as \\\"The Basterds\\\" are chosen specifically to spread fear throughout the Third Reich by scalping and brutally killing Nazis. The Basterds, lead by Lt. Aldo Raine soon cross paths with a French-Jewish teenage girl who runs a movie theater in Paris which is targeted by the soldiers.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p><span style=\\\"text-decoration: underline;\\\">Contains strong bloody violence<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"portrait_image\":\"https:\\/\\/lumiereromford.static.cinesync.io\\/images\\/movie\\/1787515925Untitled.webp\",\"landscape_image\":\"https:\\/\\/lumiereromford.static.cinesync.io\\/images\\/movie\\/1787515971716oEiFbIML_jpg_BO30,255,255,255_UF750,750_SR1910,1000,0,C_QL100_.webp\",\"url_key\":\"book-launch-event-inglourious-basterds\",\"page_link\":\"https:\\/\\/www.lumiereromford.com\\/movies\\/book-launch-event-inglourious-basterds?location=romford&locationKey=4\",\"session_start_date\":\"2026-11-20\",\"imdb_rate\":\"0.0\",\"trailer\":\"https:\\/\\/www.youtube.com\\/watch?v=sE8hc4gVyGo\",\"trailer_type\":\"1\",\"trailer_id\":\"sE8hc4gVyGo\",\"duration\":\"4h 0m\",\"movie_year\":\"2009\",\"cast\":[{\"actor\":\"Brad Pitt\"},{\"actor\":\"M\\u00e9lanie Laurent\"},{\"actor\":\"Christoph Waltz\"},{\"actor\":\"Michael Fassbender\"},{\"actor\":\"Daniel Bruhl\"},{\"actor\":\"Diane Kruger\"},{\"actor\":\"Eli Roth\"}],\"directed_by\":[{\"name\":\"Quentin Tarantino\"}],\"movie_tags\":[{\"id\":\"37\",\"name\":\"Classic cinema\",\"short_name\":\"classic\",\"description\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"70\",\"name\":\"+ Live Q&A\",\"short_name\":\"live Q&A\",\"description\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"86\",\"name\":\"Live At Lumiere\",\"short_name\":\"LIVE!\",\"description\":\"\"}],\"movie_language\":[],\"movie_certification_type_id\":\"3\",\"movie_certification_logo\":\"https:\\/\\/lumiereromford.static.cinesync.io\\/images\\/movie_certificate\\/18cert1741549184.svg\",\"movie_certification_name\":\"18\",\"movie_certification_short_code\":\"18\",\"movie_certification_description\":\"\",\"is_restricted_mode\":false,\"is_booking_open\":true,\"is_coming_soon\":false,\"is_this_sold_by_third_party_system\":\"1\",\"third_party_system_url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.waterstones.com\\/events\\/inglourious-ba